        <fig id="nurse-article-29550.image.f1" position="float" orientation="portrait">
          <caption>
            <p>Hemorrhagic Stroke Process. The illustration shows how a hemorrhagic stroke can occur in the brain. An aneurysm in a cerebral artery breaks open, which causes bleeding in the brain. The pressure of the blood causes brain tissue death. National Heart Lung and Blood Institute&#x000a0;</p>
          </caption>
          <graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="Stroke_hemorrhagic" position="float" orientation="portrait"/>
